 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 02. Data Preparation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This notebook will be used to prepare the input data for the ClearCNV model. We will load the `SpatialData` object, explore it, and then prepare the three required inputs for the model:\n",
    "1. Gene expression matrix\n",
    "2. Spatial graph\n",
    "3. Gene bins"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import spatialdata as sd\n",
    "import numpy as np"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load the SpatialData object"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_dir = \"../data\"\n",
    "sdata_path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"Xenium5K_human_prostate.zarr\")\n",
    "sdata = sd.read_zarr(sdata_path)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(sdata)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Explore the SpatialData object"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now that we have loaded the `SpatialData` object, we can explore its contents. A `SpatialData` object can contain multiple elements, such as images, tables, and shapes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Images: {list(sdata.images.keys())}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Tables: {list(sdata.tables.keys())}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Shapes: {list(sdata.shapes.keys())}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.1. Gene Expression Matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The gene expression data is stored in the `table` element. We can access it and convert it to a torch tensor."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "expression_matrix = sdata.table.X.toarray()\n",
    "print(f\"Expression matrix shape: {expression_matrix.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2. Spatial Graph"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To build the spatial graph, we need the spatial coordinates of the cells. These are stored in the `shapes` element."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cell_coords = sdata.shapes[\"cell_boundaries\"].geometry.centroid.array\n",
    "print(f\"Cell coordinates shape: {cell_coords.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we can build a spatial graph. A common approach is to use a k-nearest neighbors (k-NN) graph."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.neighbors import kneighbors_graph\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build the k-NN graph\n",
    "n_neighbors = 6\n",
    "spatial_graph = kneighbors_graph(cell_coords, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, mode='connectivity', include_self=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert to a dense torch tensor\n",
    "spatial_graph_tensor = torch.from_numpy(spatial_graph.toarray())\n",
    "print(f\"Spatial graph shape: {spatial_graph_tensor.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.3. Gene Bins"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To create the gene bins, we need information about the genomic location of each gene. This information is often stored in the `sdata.table.var` dataframe."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gene_info = sdata.table.var\n",
    "print(gene_info.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we need to define a strategy to bin the genes. For example, we can bin them by chromosome."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gene_bins = {}\n",
    "for i, gene in enumerate(gene_info.index):\n",
    "    # This is a placeholder. You will need to adapt this to your data.\n",
    "    # We assume that the gene name contains chromosome information, e.g. 'CHR1-GENE'\n",
    "    if \"-\" in gene:\n",
    "        chromosome = gene.split(\"-\", 1)[0]\n",
    "        if chromosome not in gene_bins:\n",
    "            gene_bins[chromosome] = []\n",
    "        gene_bins[chromosome].append(i)"
   ]
  }
